From: Sergey Strebulaev <s@vivantel.dev>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:57:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] fix: lint findings - missing frontmatter fields, one
 dangling ref

Every guardrail in this repo has stated its derivation in a `##
Derivation` prose section since the day guardrail-derivation-fields.md
was written, but none of them - including that guardrail, about
itself - ever actually carried governed-by/grounded-in/derivation-note
as real frontmatter fields, which is what it explicitly requires
("structured, machine-checkable... not only a prose convention").
Same gap on the fact side: all 5 pre-existing facts predate
fact-governance-fields.md and were never retrofitted with kind/
governed-by. Running kms's own lint skill against kms's own repo
caught both systemic gaps, plus one real dangling reference (a fact
pointing at a guardrail that was split and deleted, missing the
"since deleted" annotation the other similar cases already have) and
one orphaned fact now cross-referenced from its owning decision.

Six of the eight guardrails' actual "descriptive basis" turned out to
be another decision or guardrail, not a fact - grounded-in: TBD for
those rather than force-fitting a non-fact into a field that's
supposed to hold one.

Refs: docs/guardrails/fact-governance-fields.md
Refs: docs/guardrails/guardrail-derivation-fields.md
